1. What does the --release argument in Cargo do when added to a build and run?
This flag sets the cargo run to release mode, which gives longer compilation time for better optimizations and performance in our binary.
2. How can you enable an enum or struct to be passed into the println! macro?
Just implement std::fmt::Display for your struct or enum and you are good to go!
3. In nanoservices, how does a basic service help keep technical debt down?
By splitting responsibilites across different services you get decoupled, easy to refactor and easy to change (ETC) code.
4. How does returning the same error type in functions reduce the amount of code we write?
We don't need to match every possible error, but just check it by question mark or single check I guess.
5. How do we point to another Cargo project so we can compile that Cargo project into another Cargo project?
Just set it as a dependency in Cargo.toml [dependencies] section and provide a path to your another crate if it is in the same workspace, otherwise provide version to download it from crates.io.
6. If we have a Cargo project, how can we choose to include an optional dependency to be compiled into out project?
By setting optional = true when defining a dependency, for example:
serde_json = { version = "1", optional = true }

1. What parameter is passed to HttpServer::new function and what does the parameter return?
To HttpServer::new function is passed a factory function (usually closure) that constructs our http server by constructing App struct with routes, ServiceConfig, etc.
2. How can we work out what data types an API function can return automatically?
